---
// What Misha keeps, where, and what it sends to other services, for anyone: the landing page's footer and FAQ link
// here. Keep it in step with what the Misha app keeps under ~/.misha (misha-desktop's README).
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'
import Canvas from '../layouts/Canvas.astro'

const KEPT = [
  [
    'Your settings: my icon, personality and notes, the people I leave alone or take work from, the channels I watch and the repositories I work in',
    'misha.db',
    'To answer the way you asked',
  ],
  [
    'Slack messages waiting for me, and a record of each post I made',
    'misha.db',
    'To answer each message once and know which posts are mine',
  ],
  [
    'My own copies of the repositories I read, and my helpers’ worktrees',
    'Folders next to it',
    'To work on code without touching your own checkouts',
  ],
] as const

const OTHERS = [
  [
    'Anthropic',
    'gets what each Claude Code turn works with: the Slack messages I answer, the code I read and what my tools found. It runs on your own plan, exactly as when you use Claude Code yourself, including what your organization can see on a Team or Enterprise plan.',
  ],
  ['OpenAI', 'gets the same for a helper on a GPT model, only if you add a GPT sign-in, through your own OpenCode sign-in.'],
  ['Slack', 'gets what I post and upload. I read and post through your signed-in Slack tab, and Slack’s terms cover it.'],
  [
    'Services you connect',
    '(GitHub, Google, Figma, Fireflies, AWS, Atlassian) get the requests I make there and what they carry, with your own sign-in.',
  ],
] as const
---

<Canvas title="Privacy">
  <article class="dd-card dd-privacy">
    <h1 class="heading-1">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="dd-muted body-l">
      The app runs on your Mac and keeps its own data there. This page says what it keeps, where, and what goes to the
      services you use.
    </p>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">Your Mac, not my server</h2>
      <p>
        There is no Dumdum Misha server: I run no backend of my own. My own data is in one folder on your Mac,
        <code class="dd-code">~/.misha</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        My conversations run in your own Claude Code, so Claude Code keeps them where it keeps your other sessions. A
        helper on a GPT model runs in OpenCode, which keeps its sessions among yours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">What I keep in ~/.misha</h2>
      <table class="dd-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>What</th><th>Where</th><th>Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            KEPT.map(([what, where, why]) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{what}</td>
                <td>{where}</td>
                <td>{why}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">What I never see</h2>
      <ul class="dd-list">
        <li>
          <Icon name="x" /><span
            >Your Slack token and cookies. I work through your Slack tab, and they never reach me, my helpers or my
            logs.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <Icon name="x" /><span>Your Claude Code sign-in. I check that you’re signed in and never read the token.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">What goes to other services</h2>
      <p>To do the work, I send what it needs to the services you already use, under your accounts and their terms.</p>
      <ul class="dd-list">
        {
          OTHERS.map(([who, what]) => (
            <li>
              <Icon name="dot" />
              <span>
                <b>{who}</b> {what}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">This website</h2>
      <p>
        A static page, hosted by Vercel, with its domain at Cloudflare: no sign-in, no forms, no cookies, no trackers.
        Asking for an invite is an ordinary email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="dd-sec">
      <h2 class="heading-2">Deleting</h2>
      <p>
        Quit Misha and delete <code class="dd-code">~/.misha</code>, and my own data is gone. My conversations stay in
        Claude Code, and a GPT helper’s in OpenCode, until you delete them there. Deleting files on your Mac doesn’t
        delete what I already posted or uploaded to Slack or what connected services keep, and it leaves your sign-ins
        to them as they are. There’s no account to close.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Canvas>

<style>
  .dd-privacy {
    max-width: 820px;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .dd-privacy .dd-table {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .dd-privacy .dd-sec > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
